ed": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 967, "output_tokens": 294, "latency_ms": 12944.602999999915, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "用户想要为PT101配置高限报警，阈值2.0，中等优先级。当前阶段是ANALYZE_INTENT，可用工具是manage_pages和manage_points。我们需要先分析意图：用户想要配置报警，这属于CONFIG_ALARM阶段，但当前阶段不是CONFIG_ALARM。我们需要切换到CONFIG_ALARM阶段。不过，首先我们需要确认PT101这个点是否存在。我们可以先调用manage_points来列出所有点，或者按类型筛选。但用户只提供了点名PT101。我们需要先确认这个点是否存在，然后再配置报警。然而，当前阶段的可用工具只有manage_pages和manage_points，它们都只能执行list操作。CONFIG_ALARM阶段才应该有配置报警的工具。因此，我们需要切换到CONFIG_ALARM阶段。但根据行为准则，若当前阶段的可用工具不满足需求，可以在回复的纯文本中包含\"next_state: 阶段名\"来切换到合适的阶段。所以，我应该先切换到CONFIG_ALARM阶段。不过，也许我需要先确认点是否存在。但manage_points的list_points功能可以查询点信息。我可以先调用manage_points来检查PT101是否存在，然后再切换到CONFIG_ALARM阶段。这样更稳妥。先调用manage_points列出所有点。"}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2187, "output_tokens": 291, "latency_ms": 9681.259900000441, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "现在我已经确认了PT101这个点存在，类型是analog（模拟量），这正是我们需要的。用户要求配置高限报警，阈值2.0，中等优先级。我需要为PT101创建一个模拟量报警，设置高限为2.0，中等优先级。\n\n根据manage_alarms工具，我需要调用create_analog_alarm动作。需要提供以下参数：\n- action: \"create_analog_alarm\"\n- id: 需要一个唯一的报警ID，我可以使用类似\"alarm_PT101_high\"的格式\n- tag: \"PT101\"\n- high_limit: 2.0\n- low_limit: null（用户只要求高限）\n- deadband: 0.0（默认值）\n- priority: \"medium\"（中等优先级）\n\n现在我可以调用manage_alarms工具来创建报警了。"}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2552, "output_tokens": 122, "latency_ms": 2907.3607999998785, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The error indicates that `low_limit` should be a number or null, but I passed `\"None\"` as a string. Let me correct this by not passing `low_limit` at all (since it has a default of null)."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4698, "output_tokens": 105, "latency_ms": 4543.174100001124, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "Let me try explicitly setting low_limit to null (as JSON null, not the string \"None\")."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4877, "output_tokens": 127, "latency_ms": 5653.577600000062, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The parameter specification says low_limit has a default of null. I need to pass it as JSON null. Let me try again without the low_limit parameter at all - it should use the default value."}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5078, "output_tokens": 342, "latency_ms": 10781.91660000084, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "Let me try setting low_limit to a specific null value. The schema says it accepts number or null. Maybe I need to pass an actual null value somehow. Let me try passing low_limit as an empty string or some other value.\n\nActually, looking at the error, it seems like the system is having trouble with the null type. Let me try a different approach - maybe I should set low_limit to a very small number like -9999 or simply try passing it as explicitly null in a different way. Let me try with low_limit set to 0 or a negative number.\n\nActually wait - looking at the schema more carefully:\n```\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}\n```\n\nIt says `anyOf` number or null. The error says \"unable to parse string as a number\" which suggests that somewhere the null is being converted to a string \"None\". \n\nLet me try to not include low_limit at all and see if the default works. But I already tried that...\n\nLet me try with low_limit set to a specific number value to see if that works."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5494, "output_tokens": 112, "latency_ms": 4826.581799999985, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The issue seems to be with the parameter passing. Let me try passing low_limit with a numeric value directly. The problem might be in how null is being interpreted. Let me try with just the minimum required parameters and see if that works."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5680, "output_tokens": 273, "latency_ms": 8261.678799999572, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "This is very strange - the error keeps occurring even with different parameter combinations. The error message says \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" but I haven't explicitly set low_limit in some attempts.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach - maybe there's an issue with the tool schema. Let me try setting low_limit to a very specific numeric value to make sure it gets parsed correctly. Maybe I should use -999 or some very low number.\n\nActually, wait - I notice something. Every time I call the function, the system is adding low_limit as a parameter even when I don't specify it. This might be a system issue where it's converting the default null to a string \"None\" somewhere.\n\nLet me try one more approach - setting low_limit to a specific number like -100 or 0 to see if that bypasses the null handling issue."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 15, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 31533, "output_tokens": 1666, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 61105.837000000975}, "judge": null}
