r that:\n1. No points are configured yet\n2. No history tags are set up\n\nI should ask the user if they want to:\n1. First add the condenser outlet points\n2. Then configure history logging for those points\n\nActually, wait - I'm now in the CONFIG_HISTORY phase and my available tools are only `manage_history`. But there are no points configured at all. \n\nLet me check the `manage_history` tool - it has `query_history` and `list_history` actions. The `query_history` action requires a tag name.\n\nSince there are no points and no history configured, I cannot query any data. I should inform the user about this situation.\n\nActually, looking at the query_history action more carefully - it says \"Read a synthetic historical window for a tag (deterministic sine-wave demo).\" This suggests it's a demo/synthetic data function. Let me try to use it with a tag name related to \"冷凝器出口\".\n\nBut I don't know the exact tag name. The previous list showed 0 points, so there's nothing configured. I should inform the user that:\n1. There are currently no points configured\n2. There are no history logging configurations\n3. We need to first configure points and set up history logging before we can query trend data\n\nI should suggest switching to CONFIG_POINT phase to add the condenser outlet points first."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 15, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "HistoryQuery"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 2169, "output_tokens": 828, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 30016.579600000114}, "judge": null}
