gh_limit=100, low_limit=null, deadband=0, priority=\"high\"\n2. LL 报警：id=\"alarm_TI-201_LL\", tag=\"TI-201\", high_limit=null, low_limit=10, deadband=0, priority=\"high\"\n\n不过，我需要考虑死区(deadband)设置。用户没有指定死区，我可以使用默认值0。\n\n让我开始创建第一个报警。"}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2741, "output_tokens": 253, "latency_ms": 8455.380600000353, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我得到一个模式错误：`low_limit` 应该是一个数字或 null，但我传递了 `None`（作为字符串）。我需要将其设为 `null`。在 JSON 中，我应该使用 `null` 而不是 `None`。让我重试。首先创建 HH 报警，将 `low_limit` 设为 `null`。然后创建 LL 报警。我需要确保正确传递 `null`。在参数中，我应该直接省略它，或者显式传递 `null`。根据 JSON 模式，`low_limit` 有一个默认值 `null`，所以我可以省略它。但为了清晰起见，我应该显式传递 `null`。让我重试。"}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3068, "output_tokens": 112, "latency_ms": 6489.40760000005, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The issue is that I'm passing the string \"None\" instead of a null value. Let me just omit the low_limit parameter since it has a default of null."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4822, "output_tokens": 132, "latency_ms": 5346.533899999486, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The tool is still giving an error about low_limit even though I didn't provide it. Let me try explicitly setting low_limit to null using JSON null value."}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5028, "output_tokens": 241, "latency_ms": 9167.988600000172, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The issue is with the low_limit parameter. It seems like the tool expects either a number or null, but I keep passing \"None\" as a string. Let me try passing it as actual null by not including it at all, or passing a number. Since I want HH alarm only with high limit, let me just pass a very low number for low_limit like -9999 or try omitting the parameter entirely. Actually looking at the schema, it says \"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], with \"default\": null. So I should either pass a number or null. In JSON, null is represented as null, not \"None\". Let me try without including low_limit at all."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5343, "output_tokens": 129, "latency_ms": 6232.073400000445, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "Let me try providing low_limit as an actual number instead of null. I'll set it to a very low value or try different approaches."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5546, "output_tokens": 206, "latency_ms": 7111.848000000464, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "抱歉遇到工具调用问题，让我换一种方式尝试：", "reasoning": "The tool keeps rejecting the low_limit parameter with \"SCHEMA_ERROR\" saying \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\". This seems like the tool has a bug where it's not correctly handling the low_limit parameter even when I pass valid numbers or null.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe I should provide all required parameters explicitly and ensure numbers are actual numbers, not strings. Let me try again with a clean call."}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5826, "output_tokens": 232, "latency_ms": 8766.57890000024, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我尝试不传递 low_limit 参数来创建 HH 报警：", "reasoning": "The tool seems to have an issue with the low_limit parameter. Let me try using a different format - maybe the tool expects the parameters differently. Let me try with an explicit JSON number format.\n\nWait, looking at the schema more carefully: low_limit has \"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}] with default null. Let me try not providing low_limit at all for the HH alarm, and not providing high_limit for the LL alarm.\n\nActually the issue might be that I'm passing `null` as a string. In JSON, null is a special value. Let me try omitting the parameters entirely."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6132, "output_tokens": 225, "latency_ms": 7571.254200000112, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The tool keeps rejecting my calls with a schema error about low_limit. Let me try providing all required parameters with proper types. The error says \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - this suggests somewhere a string is being passed where a number is expected.\n\nLet me try with explicit numeric types for all numeric parameters and ensure I'm not accidentally passing strings.\n\nLooking at the schema again:\n- low_limit: anyOf: [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], default: null\n\nI should try not passing low_limit at all since it has a default value, or explicitly pass it as null. But in JSON, null should work.\n\nLet me try with a simpler approach - just the required fields and high_limit."}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6431, "output_tokens": 296, "latency_ms": 11900.861300000543, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我尝试显式提供一个数值类型的 low_limit 参数：", "reasoning": "The tool seems to have an issue with the schema validation for `low_limit`. Let me try passing `low_limit` as an explicit number value (0 or some value) instead of relying on the default null.\n\nLet me try:\n- HH alarm: high_limit=100, low_limit=0 (or some small number)\n- LL alarm: high_limit=200 (or some large number), low_limit=10\n\nActually, wait - the error says \"unable to parse string as a number\". This might be a tool-side issue where it's expecting the parameter but receiving a string representation of null. Let me try explicitly providing a number value for low_limit.\n\nFor HH alarm (only cares about high):\n- high_limit=100, low_limit=0\n\nFor LL alarm (only cares about low):\n- high_limit=9999, low_limit=10"}, {"turn": 12, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6801, "output_tokens": 247, "latency_ms": 8078.046199998425, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The tool keeps failing with the same error. It seems like there might be an issue with how the tool processes the parameters. Let me try a completely different approach - maybe I can use the `set_threshold` action to set thresholds on an alarm, or maybe I should try calling with minimal parameters.\n\nActually, looking at the error more carefully - it says \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\". This suggests that somewhere in the system, low_limit is being passed as a string rather than a number.\n\nLet me try passing the numbers as actual numbers (without quotes) in my function call. But wait, I've been doing that already.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach - maybe the tool has an internal issue. Let me try to call it with the absolute minimum parameters required."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 15, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 54759, "output_tokens": 2840, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 108123.26800000119}, "judge": null}
