e_points来列出所有点，看看TI-201是否在列表中。这样也能了解当前项目中有哪些点。这是一个查询类操作，是允许的。\n\n那么，我先调用manage_points来列出所有点。"}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1337, "output_tokens": 112, "latency_ms": 4602.35449999891, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "看起来type_filter需要是具体的类型，或者为null。但schema中写的是anyOf，允许null值。可能是因为我传递了\"None\"字符串，而不是JSON null。我需要传递null值。在JSON中，null应该表示为null。让我再试一次，不传递type_filter参数，因为它是可选的，默认为null。或者显式传递null。让我试试不传递type_filter。"}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2353, "output_tokens": 231, "latency_ms": 9867.622499999925, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "好的，我现在已经进入 CONFIG_ALARM 阶段了。根据当前可用工具，我需要为 TI-201 点创建 HH（高高）和 LL（低低）两个报警。\n\n用户需求：\n- 为 TI-201 点设置 HH alarm（上限报警）在 100\n- 为 TI-201 点设置 LL alarm（下限报警）在 10\n- priority 设为 high\n\nTI-201 看起来是一个温度传感器（TI 通常是 Temperature Indicator 的缩写），应该是一个模拟量点。我需要：\n\n1. 首先确认这个点是否存在 - 使用 list_points 查看\n2. 然后创建两个模拟量报警：\n   - 一个 HH 报警，high_limit = 100\n   - 一个 LL 报警，low_limit = 10\n\n让我先列出所有点来确认 TI-201 是否存在。"}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4224, "output_tokens": 366, "latency_ms": 9888.696400001209, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我现在处于 **CONFIG_ALARM** 阶段，可以直接为 TI-201 创建报警了。我将创建两个模拟量报警：HH（高高限 100）和 LL（低低限 10），优先级均为 high。", "reasoning": "The user wants to create HH (High-High) and LL (Low-Low) alarms for tag TI-201:\n- HH alarm at 100, priority high\n- LL alarm at 10, priority high\n\nI'm now in CONFIG_ALARM stage, so I have access to the manage_alarms tool. I can create two analog alarms:\n1. One for the high-high limit (HH) at 100\n2. One for the low-low limit (LL) at 10\n\nLet me create both alarms using create_analog_alarm action."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4709, "output_tokens": 232, "latency_ms": 8633.286799999041, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "上次传参有误，我需要省略不需要的限值参数，让它们默认为 null。", "reasoning": "The schema shows that high_limit and low_limit accept `anyOf: [number, null]` with default null. The issue is that \"None\" was being passed as a string. I should simply omit those parameters or pass null properly. Let me try without specifying the limits that aren't needed."}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5060, "output_tokens": 255, "latency_ms": 7756.24070000049, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我尝试正确传递参数，将不需要的限值显式设为 null。", "reasoning": "I need to pass the parameters correctly. When I omit the parameters, it seems the system is having issues. Let me try passing explicit null values in the correct format. The schema says high_limit and low_limit accept `anyOf: [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]`. I should pass null as a JSON null value."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5436, "output_tokens": 410, "latency_ms": 10620.766100000765, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "明白了，问题是我在传递参数时使用了 \"None\" 字符串而不是真正的 null 值。让我重新尝试，只传递需要的参数，省略不需要的限值（默认为 null）。", "reasoning": "The issue is that I'm passing \"None\" as a string, but the schema expects either a number or null (JSON null). Let me try omitting the parameters entirely that I don't need - the defaults should handle them.\n\nActually, looking at the schema more carefully:\n- high_limit: anyOf: [number, null], default: null\n- low_limit: anyOf: [number, null], default: null\n\nSo I should just not include the ones I don't need. Let me try again by only specifying the required parameters plus the limit I want.\n\nWait, the error says \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - this suggests \"None\" is being passed as a string. I need to figure out how to pass null in the tool call.\n\nLet me try using the JSON literal null value. In the function call format, I should just not include the parameter at all since it has a default of null."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5965, "output_tokens": 282, "latency_ms": 8145.731300000989, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我尝试完全省略不需要的参数字段，不传 null 值。", "reasoning": "I need to figure out how to pass null values properly. The schema says the fields accept `anyOf: [number, null]` with default null. Let me try not passing those fields at all and see if it works.\n\nFor the HH alarm, I only need high_limit=100, so I shouldn't pass low_limit at all.\nFor the LL alarm, I only need low_limit=10, so I shouldn't pass high_limit at all."}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6366, "output_tokens": 193, "latency_ms": 10267.922300001374, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "好的，让我这次完全不传递不需要的参数字段，只传必需的和需要设定的值：", "reasoning": "Let me try omitting the unnecessary fields entirely - just not including them at all in the function call parameters."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6678, "output_tokens": 607, "latency_ms": 17896.67550000013, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我尝试显式传递 JSON 的 `null` 值：", "reasoning": "I keep getting the same error. Let me look at the error more carefully.\n\nFor the HH alarm (high_limit=100):\n- Error: \"create_analog_alarm.low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"\n\nFor the LL alarm (low_limit=10):\n- Error: \"create_analog_alarm.high_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"\n\nIt seems like even when I don't pass low_limit or high_limit, there's some default value being passed that's a string. The schema says the defaults are null, but maybe there's an issue with how the defaults are being handled.\n\nWait - I notice in the JSON schema, high_limit and low_limit have defaults of null. But maybe the issue is that I'm still somehow passing string \"None\" somewhere. Let me look at my function calls again...\n\nActually, looking at the error, it says for the HH alarm, the issue is with low_limit, and for the LL alarm, the issue is with high_limit. These are the ones I'm NOT specifying. But the defaults should be null...\n\nHmm, maybe I need to actually pass both parameters with their intended values. For the HH alarm, I could try setting low_limit to a very low number like -9999, and for the LL alarm, set high_limit to 9999. But that's not ideal.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe I need to pass null as a JSON null explicitly. In JSON, null is represented as `null` (lowercase). Let me try that.\n\nActually wait, I realize the issue. When I write `<parameter name=\"low_limit\">None</parameter>`, it's being parsed as a string \"None\" rather than JSON null. And when I omit the parameter, maybe there's some issue with how the system handles the default.\n\nLet me try to explicitly pass `null` in JSON format."}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 7404, "output_tokens": 494, "latency_ms": 17448.70120000087, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "看起来系统对 null 值处理有问题。让我换一种方式——为 HH 报警设置一个实际的低限值，为 LL 报警设置一个实际的高限值，使它们不会干扰实际报警：", "reasoning": "I keep getting the same error. The system is having trouble with null values. Let me think about this differently.\n\nFor the HH alarm, I need high_limit=100 and don't need low_limit.\nFor the LL alarm, I need low_limit=10 and don't need high_limit.\n\nMaybe I should try a different approach - use the same limit for both but with a value that makes sense. For HH alarm, I could set low_limit to something like 0 or -273 (absolute zero) as a practical lower bound. For LL alarm, I could set high_limit to something like 9999 as a practical upper bound.\n\nOr, maybe I should try passing both alarms with both limits set to reasonable values:\n- HH alarm: high_limit=100, low_limit=0 (or some low value)\n- LL alarm: high_limit=9999 (or some high value), low_limit=10\n\nActually, looking at typical SCADA alarm configurations, it's common to have a single alarm with both high and low limits. But the user specifically asked for separate HH and LL alarms.\n\nLet me try setting the unused limits to extreme but numeric values. For HH, set low_limit to -999. For LL, set high_limit to 9999."}, {"turn": 12, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 8017, "output_tokens": 822, "latency_ms": 30821.04470000013, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我注意到错误信息总是指向我没有明确传值的参数。让我尝试将所有参数都显式传入，使用浮点数格式：", "reasoning": "I keep getting the same error message. The error says \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" for the parameter I'm NOT specifying. This is very strange.\n\nWait - looking at the error messages again:\n- For HH alarm (high_limit=100, low_limit=-999): Error on low_limit\n- For LL alarm (high_limit=9999, low_limit=10): Error on high_limit\n\nSo even when I pass numeric values, it's still saying it can't parse string as number? That seems like a system bug or there's something wrong with how I'm passing the parameters.\n\nLet me re-read the schema carefully:\n```json\n\"high_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"High Limit\"},\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"},\n```\n\nThe types are number or null. I've been passing numbers like 100, -999, 9999, 10...\n\nWait, maybe the issue is with the type of number? In JSON, numbers can be integer or float. The schema says `type: \"number\"` which should accept both.\n\nHmm, but the error message is consistent - it's always the parameter that's supposed to be null that fails. When I omit a parameter, the system might be passing a default value incorrectly.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach. What if I create both alarms with both high and low limits explicitly set?\n\nFor HH alarm: high_limit=100, low_limit=10 (same as LL)\nFor LL alarm: high_limit=100, low_limit=10 (same as HH)\n\nNo that doesn't make sense either.\n\nActually wait - what if the issue is that the system is somehow interpreting my omitted parameters as empty strings? The error says \"unable to parse string as a number\". Maybe when a parameter is omitted, the system passes an empty string instead of null?\n\nLet me try passing all parameters explicitly with actual numbers. For the HH alarm, I'll set low_limit to a very low number. For the LL alarm, I'll set high_limit to a very high number. But I already tried that...\n\nActually, let me re-examine. When I passed:\n```\nhigh_limit: 100\nlow_limit: -999\n```\nThe error was on low_limit saying \"unable to parse string as a number\". But -999 IS a number...\n\nUnless the system is not receiving my parameters correctly. Maybe there's a format issue.\n\nLet me try with explicit decimal points:\n- high_limit: 100.0\n- low_limit: -999.0"}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 15, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 58523, "output_tokens": 4317, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 147967.63310000097}, "judge": null}
{"trace_id": "8238c22b-8b86-4764-bf1a-eb8f36a48692", "experiment": {"config_name": "D_hier_rag_workflow", "config_hash": "sha256:475acf1b138c3254241ea5bc9e3026b3872809cbc539ca060c86f7f668b25a23", "code_commit": "6c299a18e517871b834f2a6226522e7c6e6c6e40", "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "dataset_version": "dev", "rep_index": 2, "seed": 44}, "query": {"golden_id": "golden-016", "text": "在chemical screen加个tank，绑到TI-201上，另外加个button用于start", "complexity": "medium", "domain": "graphics"}, "execution": {"started_at": "2026-06-16T06:41:32.525Z", "completed_at": "2026-06-16T06:43:00.523Z", "total_turns": 5, "terminal_state": "BIND_POINTS", "early_terminated": false, "termination_reason": null}, "states": [{"name": "MANAGE_PAGES", "entered_at": "2026-06-16T06:41:32.525Z", "exited_at": "2026-06-16T06:41:43.665Z"}, {"name": "GENERATE_LAYOUT", "entered_at": "2026-06-16T06:41:43.665Z", "exited_at": "2026-06-16T06:42:06.890Z"}, {"name": "MANAGE_PAGES", "entered_at": "2026-06-16T06:42:06.890Z", "exited_at": "2026-06-16T06:42:14.148Z"}, {"name": "BIND_POINTS", "entered_at": "2026-06-16T06:42:14.148Z", "exited_at": "2026-06-16T06:43:00.523Z"}], "tool_calls": [{"turn": 1, "state": "MANAGE_PAGES", "visible_tools": [{"name": "manage_pages", "allowed_actions": ["create_widget", "create_page", "list_pages"]}], "visible_count": 1, "selected": "manage_pages", "action": "list_pages", "args": {"action": "list_pages"}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": true, "error_code": "OK", "error_msg": null, "result_data": {"count": 1, "pages": [{"id": "chem_screen", "name": "chemical screen"}]}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 1.3902999999118038, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}, {"turn": 3, "state": "MANAGE_PAGES", "visible_tools": [{"name": "manage_graphics", "allowed_actions": ["create_text", "create_line", "group_widgets", "set_widget_style", "apply_flow_layout"]}, {"name": "manage_pages", "allowed_actions": ["list_pages"]}], "visible_count": 2, "selected": "manage_pages", "action": "list_pages", "args": {"action": "list_pages"}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": true, "error_code": "OK", "error_msg": null, "result_data": {"count": 1, "pages": [{"id": "chem_screen", "name": "chemical screen"}]}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 1.3810000000376021, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}, {"turn": 4, "state": "BIND_POINTS", "visible_tools": [{"name": "manage_pages", "allowed_actions": ["bind_point", "list_pages"]}, {"name": "manage_points", "allowed_actions": ["list_points"]}], "visible_count": 2, "selected": "manage_points", "action": "list_points", "args": {"action": "list_points"}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": true, "error_code": "OK", "error_msg": null, "result_data": {"count": 2, "points": [{"tag": "TI-201", "type": "analog", "unit": null, "min": null, "max": null, "description": null}, {"tag": "CMD_START", "type": "digital", "unit": null, "min": null, "max": null, "description": null}]}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 0.778899999204441, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}, {"turn": 4, "state": "BIND_POINTS", "visible_tools": [{"name": "manage_pages", "allowed_actions": ["bind_point", "list_pages"]}, {"name": "manage_points", "allowed_actions": ["list_points"]}], "visible_count": 2, "selected": "manage_pages", "action": "list_pages", "args": {"action": "list_pages"}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": true, "error_code": "OK", "error_msg": null, "result_data": {"count": 1, "pages": [{"id": "chem_screen", "name": "chemical screen"}]}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 0.6820999988121912, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}, {"turn": 4, "state": "VALIDATE", "visible_tools": [], "visible_count": 0, "selected": "workflow:handlers.validate_project", "action": null, "args": {}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": true, "error_code": "OK", "error_msg": null, "result_data": {"ok": true, "checked_at": "validate_project"}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 0.0035000011848751456, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:fcecac1dae4dfaf00fb3049afcbdce0448e44c2f01436ef07ea9f3346a61faab", "final_hash": "sha256:fcecac1dae4dfaf00fb3049afcbdce0448e44c2f01436ef07ea9f3346a61faab", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1298, "output_tokens": 97, "latency_ms": 11135.837699999684, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我先查看一下现有的页面列表，找到 chemical screen 的页面 ID。", "reasoning": "The user wants to:\n1. Add a tank widget on the \"chemical screen\" page, bound to point TI-201\n2. Add a button widget for \"start\"\n\nFirst, I need to list the existing pages to find the \"chemical screen\" page ID."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2056, "output_tokens": 778, "latency_ms": 23220.33080000074, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "很抱歉，我需要向您说明当前的限制：\n\n---\n\n**当前阶段（GENERATE_LAYOUT）的可用工具不支持创建 Tank 和 Button 控件。**\n\n当前 `manage_graphics` 工具仅支持以下操作：\n| 操作 | 说明 |\n|------|------|\n| `create_text` | 创建静态文本标签 |\n| `create_line` | 绘制线条（如管道） |\n| `group_widgets` | 将已有控件分组 |\n| `set_widget_style` | 设置控件样式 |\n| `apply_flow_layout` | 流式布局排列 |\n\n---\n\n**无法完成的操作：**\n1. ❌ **创建 Tank 控件** — 当前没有创建 Tank 等复杂工业控件的工具\n2. ❌ **创建 Button 控件** — 当前没有创建按钮的工具\n3. ❌ **绑定点位 TI-201** — 点位绑定功能需要切换到 `BIND_POINTS` 阶段\n\n---\n\n**建议：**\n- 切换到 **MANAGE_PAGES** 阶段，该阶段可能提供更完整的控件创建能力\n- 或者切换到 **BIND_POINTS** 阶段进行点位绑定\n\n请问您希望我切换到哪个阶段继续操作？或者如果您已经在其他阶段完成了 Tank 和 Button 控件的创建，我可以帮您进行后续的分组、样式设置或布局排列。\n\nnext_state: MANAGE_PAGES", "reasoning": "The user wants to:\n1. Add a tank widget on the \"chemical screen\" page, bound to point TI-201\n2. Add a button widget for \"start\"\n\nI found the page ID is \"chem_screen\". Now I need to create these widgets. However, looking at my available tools:\n\n1. `manage_graphics` - has actions: create_text, create_line, group_widgets, set_widget_style, apply_flow_layout\n2. `manage_pages` - has action: list_pages\n\nThe problem is:\n- I don't have a tool to create a \"tank\" widget - there's no create_tank or similar action\n- I don't have a tool to create a \"button\" widget - there's no create_button or similar action\n- I don't have a tool to bind points to widgets in this stage (that would be BIND_POINTS stage)\n\nThe manage_graphics tool only supports: create_text, create_line, group_widgets, set_widget_style, apply_flow_layout. None of these can create a tank or button widget.\n\nSince the current stage (GENERATE_LAYOUT) doesn't have the appropriate tools to create tank/button widgets and bind them to points, I should inform the user about this limitation.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the workflow context:\n- Current stage: GENERATE_LAYOUT\n- Next stages available: BIND_POINTS, DEPLOY, DONE, MANAGE_PAGES, VALIDATE\n\nIt seems like creating new widgets might need to happen in a different stage or the tools are limited. Let me be honest with the user - I can only create text labels and lines with the current tools. I cannot create a tank widget or a button widget.\n\nI should explain this limitation to the user and suggest switching to MANAGE_PAGES or another stage where widget creation might be possible, or explain that the current toolset doesn't support creating tank/button widgets.\n\nActually wait - let me re-read the tools. The manage_pages tool description says \"HMI page & widget management, including point↔widget binding.\" but currently only allows \"list_pages\" action. \n\nThe widget creation and point binding capabilities aren't available in this stage—I need to be straightforward with the user that the current toolset only supports text labels and lines, not tanks or buttons, and that widget binding will require moving to the BIND_POINTS stage."}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2869, "output_tokens": 204, "latency_ms": 7252.0366000007925, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我先查看一下当前页面状态：", "reasoning": "The user has entered the MANAGE_PAGES stage. However, looking at the available tools for this stage, I only have `list_pages` action available for `manage_pages` tool. \n\nLet me re-read the tool definitions:\n\nmanage_pages - \"HMI page & widget management, including point↔widget binding.\" Currently allowed actions: list_pages\n\nSo even in MANAGE_PAGES stage, I can only list pages. I cannot create widgets like tank or button, nor can I bind points.\n\nThe user wants to:\n1. Add a tank widget on \"chemical screen\" bound to TI-201\n2. Add a button for start\n\nI still don't have the tools to create widgets or bind points in this stage either. I should be honest about this limitation.\n\nLet me list the pages again and explain the situation to the user."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2428, "output_tokens": 422, "latency_ms": 20384.076299998924, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "好的，我现在进入了 BIND_POINTS 阶段。让我先确认 TI-201 点位是否存在，同时查看页面信息：", "reasoning": "Now I'm in the BIND_POINTS stage. Let me check the available tools:\n\n1. `manage_pages` - actions: bind_point, list_pages\n2. `manage_points` - actions: list_points\n\nThe user wants to:\n1. Add a tank widget bound to TI-201 on chemical screen\n2. Add a button for start\n\nHowever, I still have a problem:\n- I can bind points to existing widgets using `bind_point`\n- But I cannot CREATE new widgets like \"tank\" or \"button\" - there's no tool for that\n\nLet me first check what points exist (to verify TI-201 exists) and list the pages to see what widgets might already exist. But wait - `list_pages` only returns page IDs and names, not the widgets on those pages.\n\nActually, looking at the bind_point action, it requires:\n- page_id\n- widget_id\n- property\n- tag\n\nI need to know the widget_id to bind. But I don't have a way to create widgets or even list existing widgets.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The user is asking me to:\n1. Add a tank - this implies creating a widget\n2. Bind it to TI-201 - this is the bind_point action\n3. Add a button for start - this implies creating another widget\n\nSince I don't have a tool to create widgets, I can't complete the full request. However, I can:\n1. List points to verify TI-201 exists\n2. If somehow the widgets already exist, I could bind them\n\nLet me check what points are available first to see if TI-201 exists."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6495, "output_tokens": 793, "latency_ms": 25979.021199998897, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "好的，点位信息已确认：\n\n| 点位 | 类型 |\n|------|------|\n| `TI-201` | analog |\n| `CMD_START` | digital |\n\n---\n\n**但是，我需要向您说明当前的限制：**\n\n当前可用工具中 **没有创建控件（Widget）的功能**。我能做的操作如下：\n\n| 工具 | 可用操作 |\n|------|----------|\n| `manage_pages` | `bind_point`（绑定点位到已有控件）、`list_pages` |\n| `manage_points` | `list_points` |\n| `manage_graphics` | `create_text`、`create_line`、`group_widgets`、`set_widget_style` |\n\n**没有** `create_widget`、`create_tank`、`create_button` 等控件创建工具。\n\n---\n\n**可选方案：**\n\n1. **如果您已有 Tank 和 Button 控件**（通过其他途径创建），请告诉我它们的 `widget_id`，我可以帮您将 `TI-201` 绑定到 Tank，将 `CMD_START` 绑定到 Button。\n\n2. **如果尚未创建控件**，我无法在当前工具集下完成 Tank/Button 的创建。建议您在项目配置工具（如图形编辑器）中先创建控件，然后我再帮您完成绑定。\n\n请问您是否已有现成的控件？或者您希望我用文本标签（`create_text`）作为临时占位？", "reasoning": "Now I have the information I need:\n- Page: \"chem_screen\" (chemical screen)\n- Points exist: \"TI-201\" (analog) and \"CMD_START\" (digital)\n\nHowever, the problem is that I still cannot CREATE widgets. The `manage_pages` tool in BIND_POINTS stage only has these actions:\n- bind_point: Bind a tag to a widget property\n- list_pages: List all pages\n\nI can bind points to existing widgets, but I cannot create new widgets like \"tank\" or \"button\".\n\nWait, let me re-read the tool definition more carefully:\n\n```\nmanage_pages - \"HMI page & widget management, including point↔widget binding.\"\nCurrently allowed actions: bind_point, list_pages\n```\n\nThe tool doesn't have create_widget action. I don't have any tool to create widgets.\n\nActually, I need to be honest with the user. The current toolset doesn't include a way to:\n1. Create a tank widget\n2. Create a button widget\n\nI can only:\n1. List pages\n2. List points\n3. Bind existing points to existing widgets (if widgets already exist)\n\nBut the user doesn't have any widgets yet on the page - there's no way for me to know if widgets exist because there's no \"list_widgets\" action.\n\nLet me explain this limitation to the user. The tools available across all stages are:\n- manage_graphics: create_text, create_line, group_widgets, set_widget_style, apply_flow_layout\n- manage_pages: bind_point, list_pages\n- manage_points: list_points\n\nNone of these allow creating a \"tank\" or \"button\" widget. The system seems to be missing widget creation capabilities.\n\nI should be transparent with the user about this limitation and suggest what we CAN do:\n1. I could create text labels as placeholders\n2. I could create lines for pipe representations\n\n\n3. Without widget creation tools, I'm unable to fulfill the request for tank and button widgets. The available functions are limited to text, lines, and layout operations, which don't include the industrial control widgets needed here.\n\nI could use text labels as placeholders for what would be tank and button widgets, then bind the appropriate points to them—though this wouldn't provide the actual interactive functionality or visual representation that real widgets would offer."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 15, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "ChemicalProductionScreen"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 15146, "output_tokens": 2294, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 87997.8329000005}, "judge": null}
