ss low_limit as a very negative number like -9999999.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should switch to using the set_threshold action instead? But that requires an existing alarm.\n\nActually, let me check the workflow context. I'm in CONFIG_ALARM step. The user wants to configure a high limit alarm. I need to create an analog alarm.\n\nLet me try with explicit null in JSON format. In the XML, I need to represent null somehow. Let me check if I can pass an empty string or something.\n\nActually, looking back at the attempts: when I passed \"None\" as a string, that's wrong. When I omitted low_limit, I still got the error. Maybe the tool has a bug or maybe I need to pass a number.\n\nLet me try passing low_limit as 0.0 (zero) as a number. Or maybe -1000.\n\nActually, let me think: if I want a high limit alarm at 2.0, maybe I should set low_limit to something like -1000 to ensure it doesn't interfere. That might work.\n\nLet me try with low_limit = -1000."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 15, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 60115, "output_tokens": 4222, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 107004.6642999805}, "judge": null}
